Rockchip RGA (2D accelerator) multi-core driver: kernel build glue.

Back-ported from the Rockchip develop-5.10 vendor tree and bound to the
"rockchip,rga2" node found on rk356x.  The driver sources themselves live in
the files/ overlay at drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/ (including the v5.4
for_each_sgtable_sg() backport in include/rga_version_compat.h); this patch
only hooks the new directory into the kernel build.

drivers/video/rockchip/Kconfig and drivers/video/rockchip/Makefile are created
by 317-rockchip-mpp-drivers.patch, therefore this patch must sort after it.

--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/Kconfig
@@ -9,3 +9,5 @@
 # blocks are unrelated to video decode/encode.
 #
 source "drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/Kconfig"
+
+source "drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/Kconfig"
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/Makefile
@@ -7,3 +7,8 @@
 # nothing runs unless the module is explicitly modprobed.
 #
 obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_SERVICE) += mpp/
+
+# Rockchip RGA 2D accelerator (vendor multi-core driver).  The armv8 subtarget
+# sets CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MULTI_RGA=y, so the driver is linked into vmlinux and
+# /dev/rga is registered during boot.
+obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MULTI_RGA) += rga3/
